IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- Work Health and Safety Act 2011 (Commonwealth of Australia) -- what the worker for a Commonwealth business or
-- undertaking meets: whether the Act applies to my work (ss 12, 12A) and whether I am a "worker" (s 7); the duties owed
-- to me by the business I work for (s 19) and when it must consult me (ss 47 to 49); asking for a health and safety
-- representative (s 50) and taking an unresolved issue to an inspector (ss 80, 82); stopping unsafe work, what I must
-- do then and my continuity of engagement (ss 84 to 88); my own duties (s 28) and the most I can be fined (ss 31 to 33,
-- Schedule 4); whether an incident is notifiable (ss 35 to 37); and the protection against being punished for raising
-- safety (ss 104 to 106, 112, 113, 115).
--
-- SEAT: the worker. "I work for a Commonwealth employer. What safety duties are owed to me, may I stop unsafe work, and
-- what are my duties as a worker?" The person conducting the business or undertaking (the PCBU) asks its own questions
-- in whs-seat-pcbu.l4, which calls the rules here and restates none of them.
--
-- Edition: Compilation No. 16, compilation date 1 July 2024, includes amendments up to Act No. 120, 2023 (register id
-- C2024C00243), as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/C2011A00137.txt.
--
-- PENALTIES ARE THE SCHEDULE 4 FIGURES BEFORE INDEXATION. Schedule 4 cl 4 indexes them each 1 July from 2024 by CPI
-- numbers, and the formula was lost in the deposited text's conversion; the figures here are the ones printed.
--
-- NOT ENCODED. Divisions 3 and 4 of Part 2 beyond s 28 (the designer, manufacturer, importer, supplier and installer
-- duties, ss 20 to 26); s 27 (officers) except as a penalty column; s 29; Part 4 (authorisations); Part 5 Division 3
-- beyond s 50 (work groups, elections, HSR powers), Divisions 4 and 7 (committees, provisional improvement notices);
-- s 85 (an HSR's direction is an input); Part 7 (entry permits); Parts 8 to 14 (the regulator, inspectors, notices,
-- enforceable undertakings, proceedings, review); Schedules 1 to 3. Work to which a State or Territory WHS law applies
-- answers `not covered`.
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Written from the individual's seat with the 2026-10-18 defaults. No pipeline, no coverage table, no
-- independent test pass, no human gate. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Work Health and Safety Act 2011 -- the worker's questions`

§§ `Questions this encoding does not cover`

DECLARE `Why not covered` IS ONE OF
    -- s 12(3), (9): a corresponding WHS law of a State or Territory
    `work for a business or undertaking that is not the Commonwealth's, a public authority's or a non-Commonwealth licensee's is under the State or Territory WHS law, which is not encoded (s 12)`

GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH A TYPE
DECLARE `Answer` a IS ONE OF
    `answered`    HAS `the answer` IS AN a
    `not covered` HAS `because`    IS A `Why not covered`

§§ `ss 7, 12, 12A -- does this Act apply to my work, and am I a worker`

-- s 12(1): the Act applies "(a) if the Commonwealth is conducting a business or undertaking"; "(b) if a public authority
-- is conducting a business or undertaking"; "(c) to the extent that a person is a worker and carries out work in any
-- capacity for a business or undertaking conducted by the Commonwealth or a public authority". (2): "the administration
-- of the Australian Capital Territory or the Northern Territory is not a business or undertaking conducted by the
-- Commonwealth." (4), (6): "During the transitional period for a non-Commonwealth licensee" (a body corporate that held a
-- Comcare licence under the Occupational Health and Safety Act 1991), the Act applies to work for it; the period ends on
-- a day prescribed by the regulations (an input). s 12A: the Act "does not apply in relation to any vessel ... or any
-- structure to which the Occupational Health and Safety (Maritime Industry) Act 1993 applies", nor to a facility under
-- Schedule 3 to the Offshore Petroleum and Greenhouse Gas Storage Act 2006.
-- s 4 "public authority": a Commonwealth body corporate established for a public purpose, or a Commonwealth company
-- under the PGPA Act 2013 (borrowed terms, asked as facts).
DECLARE `Who I work for` IS ONE OF
    `the Commonwealth, such as a department or agency, or the Defence Force`
    `a Commonwealth public authority or Commonwealth company`
    `a non-Commonwealth licensee (a company licensed under the Comcare scheme)`
    `the ACT or NT administration, a State or local government, or a private business`

DECLARE `Does the Act apply to my work` IS ONE OF
    `yes: this Act applies to my work for the Commonwealth or a public authority (s 12(1))`
    `yes: this Act applies to my work for a non-Commonwealth licensee in its transitional period (s 12(4))`
    `no: this Act does not apply on a vessel or structure under the Occupational Health and Safety (Maritime Industry) Act 1993, or an offshore petroleum facility (s 12A)`

@export Does the Commonwealth Work Health and Safety Act 2011 apply to my work (ss 12, 12A)?
GIVEN `who I work for` IS A `Who I work for` @desc Who conducts the business or undertaking you work for
      `the licensee is still in its transitional period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you work for a non-Commonwealth licensee: whether the day the regulations prescribe as the end of its transitional period has not yet come (ignored otherwise)
      `I work on a ship or structure under the Maritime Industry OHS Act, or an offshore petroleum facility` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the work is on a vessel or structure to which the Occupational Health and Safety (Maritime Industry) Act 1993 applies, or a facility under Schedule 3 to the Offshore Petroleum and Greenhouse Gas Storage Act 2006
GIVETH AN `Answer` `Does the Act apply to my work`
`Does the Act apply to me` MEANS
    IF `I work on a ship or structure under the Maritime Industry OHS Act, or an offshore petroleum facility`
    THEN `answered` `no: this Act does not apply on a vessel or structure under the Occupational Health and Safety (Maritime Industry) Act 1993, or an offshore petroleum facility (s 12A)`
    ELSE CONSIDER `who I work for`
         WHEN `the Commonwealth, such as a department or agency, or the Defence Force`
              THEN `answered` `yes: this Act applies to my work for the Commonwealth or a public authority (s 12(1))`
         WHEN `a Commonwealth public authority or Commonwealth company`
              THEN `answered` `yes: this Act applies to my work for the Commonwealth or a public authority (s 12(1))`
         WHEN `a non-Commonwealth licensee (a company licensed under the Comcare scheme)`
              THEN IF `the licensee is still in its transitional period`
                   THEN `answered` `yes: this Act applies to my work for a non-Commonwealth licensee in its transitional period (s 12(4))`
                   ELSE `not covered` `work for a business or undertaking that is not the Commonwealth's, a public authority's or a non-Commonwealth licensee's is under the State or Territory WHS law, which is not encoded (s 12)`
         OTHERWISE `not covered` `work for a business or undertaking that is not the Commonwealth's, a public authority's or a non-Commonwealth licensee's is under the State or Territory WHS law, which is not encoded (s 12)`

-- s 7(1): "A person is a worker if the person carries out work in any capacity for a person conducting a business or
-- undertaking, including work as: (a) an employee; (b) a contractor or subcontractor; (c) an employee of a contractor or
-- subcontractor; (d) an employee of a labour hire company who has been assigned to work in the person's business or
-- undertaking; (e) an outworker; (f) an apprentice or trainee; (g) a student gaining work experience; (h) a volunteer;
-- or (i) a person of a prescribed class." (2A): a member of the Defence Force is a worker "at work throughout the time
-- when the person is lawfully performing the functions of a member". s 5(7), (8): "A volunteer association does not
-- conduct a business or undertaking" -- a group of volunteers none of whom employs anyone to work for it.
@export Am I a "worker" of this business or undertaking under the Work Health and Safety Act (s 7)?
GIVEN `I carry out work for it in some capacity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you carry out work for this business or undertaking in any capacity: as an employee, contractor or subcontractor, a contractor's employee, a labour hire worker assigned to it, an outworker, an apprentice or trainee, a work experience student, a volunteer, or a Defence Force member performing your functions
      `it is a volunteer association with no employees` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the organisation is a group of volunteers working together for community purposes, none of whom employs anyone to carry out work for it
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I a worker` IF
        `I carry out work for it in some capacity`
    AND (NOT `it is a volunteer association with no employees`)

§§ `ss 17, 19 -- what the business I work for must ensure`

-- s 19(1): a PCBU "must ensure, so far as is reasonably practicable, the health and safety of: (a) workers engaged, or
-- caused to be engaged by the person; and (b) workers whose activities in carrying out work are influenced or directed by
-- the person; while the workers are at work". (3): "Without limiting subsections (1) and (2), ... must ensure, so far as
-- is reasonably practicable" (a) to (g). (4): accommodation it owns or controls, occupied because "other accommodation
-- is not reasonably available". s 17: the duty requires it "(a) to eliminate risks ..., so far as is reasonably
-- practicable; and (b) if it is not reasonably practicable to eliminate risks ..., to minimise those risks". s 18
-- "reasonably practicable" is a weighing the court does, not encoded.
DECLARE `Duty owed to me` IS ONE OF
    `my health and safety while at work, so far as is reasonably practicable, by eliminating risks or, if that is not reasonably practicable, minimising them (ss 17, 19(1))`
    `a work environment without risks to health and safety (s 19(3)(a))`
    `safe plant and structures (s 19(3)(b))`
    `safe systems of work (s 19(3)(c))`
    `the safe use, handling and storage of plant, structures and substances (s 19(3)(d))`
    `adequate facilities for my welfare at work, and access to them (s 19(3)(e))`
    `the information, training, instruction or supervision needed to protect me (s 19(3)(f))`
    `monitoring of my health and of conditions at the workplace to prevent illness or injury (s 19(3)(g))`
    `the accommodation it provides me, maintained so that I am not exposed to risks (s 19(4))`

@export What must the business or undertaking I work for ensure for my health and safety (ss 17, 19)?
GIVEN `it engaged me, or directs or influences my work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether this business engaged you (or caused you to be engaged), or influences or directs your activities in carrying out work
      `I live in its accommodation because nothing else is reasonably available` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you occupy accommodation it owns or manages, because the job needs it and other accommodation is not reasonably available
GIVETH A LIST OF `Duty owed to me`
`What must my employer ensure` MEANS
    IF (NOT `it engaged me, or directs or influences my work`)
    THEN EMPTY
    ELSE IF `I live in its accommodation because nothing else is reasonably available`
         THEN append `the s 19 duties` (LIST `the accommodation it provides me, maintained so that I am not exposed to risks (s 19(4))`)
         ELSE `the s 19 duties`
    WHERE
        `the s 19 duties` MEANS
            LIST `my health and safety while at work, so far as is reasonably practicable, by eliminating risks or, if that is not reasonably practicable, minimising them (ss 17, 19(1))`,
                 `a work environment without risks to health and safety (s 19(3)(a))`,
                 `safe plant and structures (s 19(3)(b))`,
                 `safe systems of work (s 19(3)(c))`,
                 `the safe use, handling and storage of plant, structures and substances (s 19(3)(d))`,
                 `adequate facilities for my welfare at work, and access to them (s 19(3)(e))`,
                 `the information, training, instruction or supervision needed to protect me (s 19(3)(f))`,
                 `monitoring of my health and of conditions at the workplace to prevent illness or injury (s 19(3)(g))`

§§ `ss 47 to 49 -- must I be consulted`

-- s 47(1): the PCBU "must, so far as is reasonably practicable, consult ... with workers who carry out work for the
-- business or undertaking who are, or are likely to be, directly affected by a matter relating to work health or
-- safety." Penalty: tier C. s 48(2): "If the workers are represented by a health and safety representative, the
-- consultation must involve that representative." s 49: consultation is required "(a) when identifying hazards and
-- assessing risks"; "(b) when making decisions about ways to eliminate or minimise those risks"; "(c) ... the adequacy
-- of facilities for the welfare of workers"; "(d) when proposing changes that may affect the health or safety of
-- workers"; "(e) when making decisions about the procedures for" consulting, resolving issues, monitoring health or
-- conditions, or information and training; "(f)" prescribed activities (an input).
DECLARE `Safety matter` IS ONE OF
    `identifying hazards or assessing risks from the work`
    `deciding how to eliminate or minimise those risks`
    `deciding whether welfare facilities are adequate`
    `proposing changes that may affect workers' health or safety`
    `deciding procedures for consultation, issue resolution, health or workplace monitoring, or information and training`
    `another activity the regulations prescribe`
    `something else`

DECLARE `Consultation` IS ONE OF
    `yes: the business must consult me, so far as is reasonably practicable, sharing the information, letting me give my views and contribute, taking them into account and telling me the outcome (ss 47, 48(1))`
    `yes: the business must consult me through my health and safety representative, who must be involved (ss 47, 48(2))`
    `no: s 49 does not list this matter, or I am not directly affected by it`

GIVEN `the matter` IS A `Safety matter`
      `the worker is, or is likely to be, directly affected` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the worker is represented by a health and safety representative` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Consultation`
`the consultation the s 47 duty needs` MEANS
    IF     (NOT `the worker is, or is likely to be, directly affected`)
        OR `the matter` EQUALS `something else`
    THEN `no: s 49 does not list this matter, or I am not directly affected by it`
    ELSE IF `the worker is represented by a health and safety representative`
         THEN `yes: the business must consult me through my health and safety representative, who must be involved (ss 47, 48(2))`
         ELSE `yes: the business must consult me, so far as is reasonably practicable, sharing the information, letting me give my views and contribute, taking them into account and telling me the outcome (ss 47, 48(1))`

@export Must the business I work for consult me about this safety matter (ss 47 to 49)?
GIVEN `the matter` IS A `Safety matter` @desc What the business is doing or deciding about health and safety
      `I am, or am likely to be, directly affected` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are, or are likely to be, directly affected by the matter
      `I am represented by a health and safety representative` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your work group has a health and safety representative
GIVETH A `Consultation`
`Must my employer consult me` MEANS
    `the consultation the s 47 duty needs` `the matter` `I am, or am likely to be, directly affected` `I am represented by a health and safety representative`

§§ `ss 50, 80, 82 -- a health and safety representative, and an issue that is not resolved`

-- s 50: "A worker who carries out work for a business or undertaking may ask the person conducting the business or
-- undertaking to facilitate the conduct of an election for 1 or more health and safety representatives".
@export May I ask the business I work for to hold an election for a health and safety representative (s 50)?
GIVEN `I carry out work for it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you carry out work for this business or undertaking, in any capacity
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I ask for an HSR election` IF `I carry out work for it`

-- s 80(1): the parties to an issue include "(c) if the worker or workers affected by the issue are in a work group, the
-- health and safety representative for that work group or his or her representative; (d) if the worker or workers ...
-- are not in a work group, the worker or workers or their representative." s 81(2): the parties "must make reasonable
-- efforts to achieve a timely, final and effective resolution" by the agreed or default procedure. s 82(1), (2): "if an
-- issue has not been resolved after reasonable efforts have been made", "A party to the issue may ask the regulator
-- [Comcare] to appoint an inspector". (3): that does not prevent a worker ceasing work under Division 6.
DECLARE `Unresolved issue` IS ONE OF
    `I may ask Comcare to appoint an inspector to help resolve it (s 82(2)); I keep my right to stop unsafe work (s 82(3))`
    `my health and safety representative, as the party for my work group, may ask Comcare to appoint an inspector (ss 80(1)(c), 82(2))`
    `not yet: the parties must first make reasonable efforts to resolve it under the agreed or default procedure (ss 81(2), 82(1))`

@export Can I take a safety issue my employer has not resolved to Comcare's inspector (ss 80 to 82)?
GIVEN `reasonable efforts to resolve it have been made` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether reasonable efforts have been made to resolve the issue under the agreed procedure, or the default procedure in the regulations
      `I am in a work group with a health and safety representative` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are in a work group that has a health and safety representative
GIVETH AN `Unresolved issue`
`Can I take the issue to an inspector` MEANS
    IF (NOT `reasonable efforts to resolve it have been made`)
    THEN `not yet: the parties must first make reasonable efforts to resolve it under the agreed or default procedure (ss 81(2), 82(1))`
    ELSE IF `I am in a work group with a health and safety representative`
         THEN `my health and safety representative, as the party for my work group, may ask Comcare to appoint an inspector (ss 80(1)(c), 82(2))`
         ELSE `I may ask Comcare to appoint an inspector to help resolve it (s 82(2)); I keep my right to stop unsafe work (s 82(3))`

§§ `ss 84 to 88 -- may I stop unsafe work`

-- s 84: "A worker may cease, or refuse to carry out, work if the worker has a reasonable concern that to carry out the work
-- would expose the worker to a serious risk to the worker's health or safety, emanating from an immediate or imminent
-- exposure to a hazard." s 85: a trained health and safety representative may direct a worker in the work group to
-- cease work on the same concern (an input). s 86: a worker who ceases work "must: (a) as soon as practicable, notify the
-- person conducting the business or undertaking that the worker has ceased work ... unless the worker ceased work under
-- a direction from a health and safety representative; and (b) remain available to carry out suitable alternative work."
-- s 87: the PCBU "may direct the worker to carry out suitable alternative work ... if that work is safe and appropriate".
DECLARE `Stopping work` IS ONE OF
    `yes: I may cease or refuse the work (s 84); I must tell the business as soon as practicable and stay available for suitable alternative work (s 86)`
    `yes: I must cease on my health and safety representative's direction (s 85); I must stay available for suitable alternative work, and need not tell the business myself (s 86)`
    `no: the right to stop work needs a reasonable concern of a serious risk to my health or safety from an immediate or imminent exposure to a hazard (s 84)`

GIVEN `I have a reasonable concern of a serious risk to my health or safety` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the risk comes from an immediate or imminent exposure to a hazard` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the s 84 right arises` IF
        `I have a reasonable concern of a serious risk to my health or safety`
    AND `the risk comes from an immediate or imminent exposure to a hazard`

@export May I stop or refuse unsafe work, and what must I do if I do (ss 84 to 86)?
GIVEN `I have a reasonable concern that the work would expose me to a serious risk to my health or safety` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have a reasonable concern that doing the work would expose you to a serious risk to your health or safety
      `the risk comes from an immediate or imminent exposure to a hazard` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether that risk comes from an immediate or imminent exposure to a hazard, not one that is remote or in the future
      `my health and safety representative has directed me to stop` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a trained health and safety representative for your work group has directed you to cease the work under s 85
GIVETH A `Stopping work`
`May I stop unsafe work` MEANS
    IF `my health and safety representative has directed me to stop`
    THEN `yes: I must cease on my health and safety representative's direction (s 85); I must stay available for suitable alternative work, and need not tell the business myself (s 86)`
    ELSE IF `the s 84 right arises` `I have a reasonable concern that the work would expose me to a serious risk to my health or safety` `the risk comes from an immediate or imminent exposure to a hazard`
         THEN `yes: I may cease or refuse the work (s 84); I must tell the business as soon as practicable and stay available for suitable alternative work (s 86)`
         ELSE `no: the right to stop work needs a reasonable concern of a serious risk to my health or safety from an immediate or imminent exposure to a hazard (s 84)`

-- s 88: ceasing work "does not affect the continuity of engagement of the worker for prescribed purposes if the worker
-- has not unreasonably failed to comply with a direction to carry out suitable alternative work: (a) at the same or
-- another workplace; and (b) that was safe and appropriate for the worker to carry out." The prescribed purposes are in
-- the regulations (not deposited).
@export If I stopped unsafe work, is my continuity of engagement protected (s 88)?
GIVEN `I was directed to safe and appropriate alternative work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the business directed you to suitable alternative work, at the same or another workplace, that was safe and appropriate for you
      `I unreasonably failed to do it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you unreasonably failed to comply with that direction (ignored if there was none)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my continuity of engagement protected` IF
    (NOT (`I was directed to safe and appropriate alternative work` AND `I unreasonably failed to do it`))

§§ `ss 28, 31 to 34, Schedule 4 -- my own duties, and the most I can be fined`

-- s 28: "While at work, a worker must: (a) take reasonable care for his or her own health and safety; and (b) take
-- reasonable care that his or her acts or omissions do not adversely affect the health and safety of other persons; and
-- (c) comply, so far as the worker is reasonably able, with any reasonable instruction that is given by the person
-- conducting the business or undertaking to allow the person to comply with this Act; and (d) co-operate with any
-- reasonable policy or procedure of the person conducting the business or undertaking relating to health or safety at
-- the workplace that has been notified to workers."
DECLARE `My duty as a worker` IS ONE OF
    `take reasonable care for my own health and safety (s 28(a))`
    `take reasonable care that my acts or omissions do not adversely affect the health and safety of others (s 28(b))`
    `comply, so far as I am reasonably able, with any reasonable instruction the business gives to comply with the Act (s 28(c))`
    `co-operate with any reasonable health or safety policy or procedure of the business that has been notified to workers (s 28(d))`

@export What are my duties as a worker while at work (s 28)?
GIVETH A LIST OF `My duty as a worker`
`What are my duties as a worker` MEANS
    LIST `take reasonable care for my own health and safety (s 28(a))`,
         `take reasonable care that my acts or omissions do not adversely affect the health and safety of others (s 28(b))`,
         `comply, so far as I am reasonably able, with any reasonable instruction the business gives to comply with the Act (s 28(c))`,
         `co-operate with any reasonable health or safety policy or procedure of the business that has been notified to workers (s 28(d))`

-- s 31: Category 1, "without reasonable excuse, engages in conduct that ... exposes an individual to whom the duty is
-- owed to a risk of death or serious injury or illness" with negligence or recklessness: "(a) In the case of an
-- individual--the category 1 monetary penalty or 15 years imprisonment or both. (b) In the case of a body corporate--the
-- category 1 monetary penalty." s 32: Category 2, a failure that "exposes an individual to a risk of death or serious
-- injury or illness". s 33: Category 3, a failure to comply. s 30A: industrial manslaughter, only by a PCBU or an officer:
-- "(a) In the case of an offence committed by an individual--25 years imprisonment. (b) In the case of an offence committed
-- by a body corporate--$18,000,000." Schedule 4 cl 1, before indexation under cl 4:
--                          column 2 (PCBU or officer)   column 3 (other individual)   column 4 (body corporate)
--   category 1             $3,000,000                   $1,500,000                    $15,000,000
--   category 2             $418,000                     $209,000                      $2,090,000
--   category 3             $140,000                     $70,000                       $700,000
DECLARE `Offence` IS ONE OF
    `industrial manslaughter: intentional conduct breaching a health and safety duty that causes a death, reckless or negligent as to it (s 30A)`
    `category 1: negligent or reckless conduct, without reasonable excuse, exposing someone to a risk of death or serious injury or illness (s 31)`
    `category 2: a failure to comply with a health and safety duty that exposes someone to a risk of death or serious injury or illness (s 32)`
    `category 3: a failure to comply with a health and safety duty (s 33)`

DECLARE `Offender` IS ONE OF
    `an individual conducting the business or undertaking, or an officer of it`
    `another individual, such as a worker`
    `a body corporate`

DECLARE `Maximum penalty` HAS
    `fine in dollars, before indexation` IS A NUMBER
    `years of imprisonment` IS A NUMBER

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN `Offence`
      `the offender` IS AN `Offender`
GIVETH A MAYBE `Maximum penalty`
`the maximum penalty` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `industrial manslaughter: intentional conduct breaching a health and safety duty that causes a death, reckless or negligent as to it (s 30A)`
         THEN CONSIDER `the offender`
              WHEN `an individual conducting the business or undertaking, or an officer of it` THEN JUST (`Maximum penalty` OF 0, 25)
              WHEN `a body corporate` THEN JUST (`Maximum penalty` OF 18000000, 0)
              OTHERWISE NOTHING
    WHEN `category 1: negligent or reckless conduct, without reasonable excuse, exposing someone to a risk of death or serious injury or illness (s 31)`
         THEN CONSIDER `the offender`
              WHEN `an individual conducting the business or undertaking, or an officer of it` THEN JUST (`Maximum penalty` OF 3000000, 15)
              WHEN `another individual, such as a worker` THEN JUST (`Maximum penalty` OF 1500000, 15)
              WHEN `a body corporate` THEN JUST (`Maximum penalty` OF 15000000, 0)
    WHEN `category 2: a failure to comply with a health and safety duty that exposes someone to a risk of death or serious injury or illness (s 32)`
         THEN CONSIDER `the offender`
              WHEN `an individual conducting the business or undertaking, or an officer of it` THEN JUST (`Maximum penalty` OF 418000, 0)
              WHEN `another individual, such as a worker` THEN JUST (`Maximum penalty` OF 209000, 0)
              WHEN `a body corporate` THEN JUST (`Maximum penalty` OF 2090000, 0)
    WHEN `category 3: a failure to comply with a health and safety duty (s 33)`
         THEN CONSIDER `the offender`
              WHEN `an individual conducting the business or undertaking, or an officer of it` THEN JUST (`Maximum penalty` OF 140000, 0)
              WHEN `another individual, such as a worker` THEN JUST (`Maximum penalty` OF 70000, 0)
              WHEN `a body corporate` THEN JUST (`Maximum penalty` OF 700000, 0)

-- A worker who fails a s 28 duty is "another individual" (column 3). s 34(1): "A volunteer does not commit an offence
-- under this Division for a failure to comply with a health and safety duty, except a duty under section 28 or 29", so a
-- volunteer worker is in the same position. Industrial manslaughter is not open against a worker (NOTHING).
@export What is the most I can be fined, or imprisoned for, if I breach my duty as a worker (ss 28, 30A to 34, Schedule 4)?
GIVEN `the offence` IS AN `Offence` @desc Which offence: category 1 (negligent or reckless conduct exposing someone to a risk of death or serious injury), category 2 (a failure that exposes someone to that risk), category 3 (any failure), or industrial manslaughter
GIVETH A MAYBE `Maximum penalty`
`What is the most I can be fined as a worker` MEANS
    `the maximum penalty` `the offence` `another individual, such as a worker`

§§ `ss 35 to 37 -- is what happened a notifiable incident`

-- s 35: "notifiable incident means: (a) the death of a person; or (b) a serious injury or illness of a person; or (c) a
-- dangerous incident." s 36: serious injury or illness means one "requiring the person to have: (a) immediate treatment
-- as an in-patient in a hospital; or (b) immediate treatment for" amputation, a serious head injury, a serious eye
-- injury, a serious burn, degloving or scalping, a spinal injury, the loss of a bodily function, serious lacerations;
-- "or (c) medical treatment within 48 hours of exposure to a substance", with any the regulations add or exclude (an
-- input). s 37: a dangerous incident is one "that exposes a worker or any other person to a serious risk to a person's
-- health or safety emanating from an immediate or imminent exposure to" an uncontrolled escape, spillage or leakage of a
-- substance; an uncontrolled implosion, explosion or fire; an uncontrolled escape of gas, steam or a pressurised
-- substance; electric shock; a fall or release from a height; the collapse or failure of authorised plant, a structure,
-- an excavation or shoring; an inrush of water, mud or gas or an interruption of ventilation underground; or a prescribed
-- event. s 38(1): the PCBU "must ensure that the regulator is notified immediately" of one "arising out of the conduct of
-- the business or undertaking".
DECLARE `What happened` IS ONE OF
    `someone died`
    `someone needed immediate treatment as a hospital in-patient`
    `someone needed immediate treatment for an amputation, a serious head or eye injury, a serious burn, degloving or scalping, a spinal injury, loss of a bodily function or serious lacerations`
    `someone needed medical treatment within 48 hours of exposure to a substance`
    `someone was exposed to a serious risk from an immediate or imminent uncontrolled escape, spill, fire, explosion, gas or steam leak, electric shock, fall from height, collapse or failure listed in s 37`
    `another injury, illness or incident`

GIVEN `what happened` IS A `What happened`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `it is a notifiable incident` IF
    (NOT (`what happened` EQUALS `another injury, illness or incident`))

@export Is what happened at work a "notifiable incident" that must be reported to Comcare at once (ss 35 to 38)?
GIVEN `what happened` IS A `What happened` @desc The most serious thing that happened: a death, an injury or illness needing the treatment listed, a dangerous incident listed in s 37, or something else
      `the regulations exclude it, or add it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Work Health and Safety Regulations exclude this kind of injury, illness or incident, or add it to the list, reversing the answer the Act gives (not encoded: false unless you know otherwise)
      `it arose out of the work of the business` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it arose out of the conduct of the business or undertaking
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is it a notifiable incident` IF
        `it arose out of the work of the business`
    AND (    (`it is a notifiable incident` `what happened` AND (NOT `the regulations exclude it, or add it`))
         OR  ((NOT `it is a notifiable incident` `what happened`) AND `the regulations exclude it, or add it`))

§§ `ss 104 to 106, 112, 113, 115 -- if I am punished for raising safety` -- arises only if the person has been dismissed or treated badly

-- s 105(1): discriminatory conduct is where the person "(a) (i) dismisses a worker; or (ii) terminates a contract for
-- services with a worker; or (iii) puts a worker to his or her detriment in the engagement of the worker; or (iv) alters
-- the position of a worker to the worker's detriment; or (b) (i) refuses or fails to offer to engage a prospective worker;
-- or (ii) treats a prospective worker less favourably", or (2) organises or threatens to. s 106: it is "for a prohibited
-- reason" if because the worker is or proposes to be an HSR or committee member, exercises or proposes to exercise a power
-- or function under the Act (stopping unsafe work under s 84 is one), assists or gives information to a person
-- exercising one, "raises or has raised or proposes to raise an issue or concern about work health and safety", is
-- involved in resolving an issue, or seeks compliance with a duty.
-- s 112(1), (6): "an eligible person" (a person affected, or their authorised representative) "may apply to a court" for
-- an injunction, compensation, reinstatement or another order. (4): only if the reason "was a substantial reason". s
-- 113(1): "must be commenced not more than 1 year after the date on which the applicant knew or ought to have known that
-- the cause of action accrued." (2): the alleged reason "is presumed to be a substantial reason ... unless the defendant
-- proves" otherwise. (3): a defence if "the conduct was reasonable in the circumstances" and "a substantial reason for the
-- conduct was to comply with the requirements of this Act". s 115(a): no proceeding "if the person has commenced a
-- proceeding or made an application or complaint in relation to the same matter under a law of the Commonwealth or a
-- State" that has not been withdrawn.
DECLARE `What was done to me` IS ONE OF
    `I was dismissed, or my contract for services was ended`
    `I was put to my detriment, or my position was altered to my detriment`
    `I was not offered the job, or offered worse terms than another applicant`
    `someone organised or threatened one of these`
    `nothing of these`

DECLARE `Why it was done` IS ONE OF
    `I am, was or proposed to be a health and safety representative or committee member, or acted as one`
    `I raised, or proposed to raise, a health or safety issue or concern`
    `I stopped unsafe work, or exercised or proposed to exercise another power or function under the Act`
    `I assisted or gave information to an inspector or someone else acting under the Act`
    `I was involved in resolving a safety issue, or sought compliance with a duty under the Act`
    `another reason`

DECLARE `Court order for discrimination` IS ONE OF
    `yes: I may apply to a court for an injunction, compensation, reinstatement or another order (s 112); the safety reason is presumed a substantial reason unless they prove otherwise (s 113(2)), and they have a defence only if the conduct was reasonable and done substantially to comply with the Act (s 113(3))`
    `no: what was done is not discriminatory conduct under s 105`
    `no: it was not done for a reason s 106 prohibits`
    `no: I have another proceeding, application or complaint about the same matter under another Commonwealth or State law that is not withdrawn (s 115(a))`

@export Can I go to court because I was dismissed or treated badly for raising a safety issue (ss 104 to 106, 112, 113, 115)?
GIVEN `what was done to me` IS A `What was done to me` @desc What the business, or another person, did or threatened to do to you
      `why it was done` IS A `Why it was done` @desc The reason you say it was done
      `I have another live claim about the same matter` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have started a proceeding, application or complaint about the same matter under another Commonwealth or State law (for example a Fair Work general protections claim) and not withdrawn it
GIVETH A `Court order for discrimination`
`Can I go to court over discrimination` MEANS
    IF `what was done to me` EQUALS `nothing of these`
    THEN `no: what was done is not discriminatory conduct under s 105`
    ELSE IF `why it was done` EQUALS `another reason`
         THEN `no: it was not done for a reason s 106 prohibits`
         ELSE IF `I have another live claim about the same matter`
              THEN `no: I have another proceeding, application or complaint about the same matter under another Commonwealth or State law that is not withdrawn (s 115(a))`
              ELSE `yes: I may apply to a court for an injunction, compensation, reinstatement or another order (s 112); the safety reason is presumed a substantial reason unless they prove otherwise (s 113(2)), and they have a defence only if the conduct was reasonable and done substantially to comply with the Act (s 113(3))`

-- s 113(1): "not more than 1 year after the date on which the applicant knew or ought to have known". The year after a day
-- ends on the same date a year on.
@export By what day must I start court proceedings over discrimination for raising safety (s 113(1))?
GIVEN `the day I knew, or ought to have known, I had a claim` IS A DATE @desc The day you knew, or ought to have known, that you had a cause of action (usually the day of the dismissal or other conduct)
GIVETH A DATE
`By when must I go to court over discrimination` MEANS `add years` `the day I knew, or ought to have known, I had a claim` 1
